{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.sym2_dim_twoJ_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.sym2_dim_twoJ_two","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L109-L112","doc":"Dimension bookkeeping at `2j = 2`: `Sym²` of the 3-dimensional adjoint has\ndimension `6 = 3·4/2`, decomposing as `5 + 1` — the singlet is present, which is\nthe gate failure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.sym2_dim_twoJ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.sym2_dim_twoJ_one","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L104-L107","doc":"Dimension bookkeeping at `2j = 1`: `Sym²` of the 2-dimensional fundamental\nhas dimension `3 = 2·3/2`, and the surviving index is `k = 1` (the spin-1\ntriplet), with the singlet absent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.self_duality_does_not_decide_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.self_duality_does_not_decide_gate","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L96-L102","doc":"**Self-duality does not decide the gate.**  Both irreps below are self-dual\n(every `SU(2)` representation is), yet one passes and one fails.  Formal record\nof the corrected inference: no predicate that holds of *all* `SU(2)` irreps can\nimply gate-failure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.adjoint_fails_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.adjoint_fails_gate","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L92-L94","doc":"The 3-dimensional adjoint (`2j = 2`, spin `1`) **fails** the gate — the case\nthe colour question actually needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.fundamental_passes_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.fundamental_passes_gate","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L87-L90","doc":"The 2-dimensional fundamental (`2j = 1`, spin `1/2`) **passes** the gate:\nits singlet sits in `Λ²`, not `Sym²`.  This is the counterexample to the\nsuperseded self-duality argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.gate_fails_iff_odd_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.gate_fails_iff_odd_dim","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**Restated in terms of the dimension.** The gate fails exactly for\nodd-dimensional irreps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.zero_mem_sym2Indices_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.zero_mem_sym2Indices_iff","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L67-L79","doc":"**The gate criterion.** The singlet index `0` survives into `Sym²(V_j)`\nexactly when `2j` is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.dimOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.dimOf","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L64-L65","doc":"The dimension of the irrep `V_j` with `2j = twoJ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.sym2Indices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateParity.sym2Indices","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateParity.lean#L58-L62","doc":"Indices `k` of the `SU(2)` irreps `V_k` occurring in `Sym²(V_j)`, where\n`twoJ = 2j`.  Clebsch–Gordan supplies `k ≤ 2j`; the symmetric square keeps\nexactly those `k` congruent to `2j` mod 2. ","signatureChunk":0}]}